## Scope

The offline, durable half of 0016. Land this first; resolver (0018)
and graph rendering (0019) build on the parsed ref kinds this
ticket exposes.

In:
- `rules/tickets.md` grammar update for `Blocked-by`.
- Validator: parse new grammar, reject malformed refs, expose
  parsed kind on the `Erg` struct.
- No network anywhere — validator stays hermetic.

Out:
- Resolution of remote state. (0018.)
- Graph/ready integration. (0018, 0019.)

## Spec change (rules/tickets.md)

Replace the `Blocked-by` row's "Values" cell with the three-form
grammar from 0016:

```
ref       := local-ref | gh-same | gh-cross
local-ref := [0-9]{4}
gh-same   := "gh#" number          # this repo
gh-cross  := "gh:" owner "/" repo "#" number
number    := [1-9][0-9]*
```

Plus the GitHub-mirroring rules for `owner` and `repo` (see 0016).

Resolve Deferred #1 from 0016 (bare `gh#N` fork-renaming) before
this PR merges — the spec text needs to commit one way.

## Validator changes (`tickets/tools/go`)

1. Extend the `Blocked-by` parser to recognize all three ref forms.
2. Reject malformed refs with a precise message:
   - `gh:` without `owner/repo#N`.
   - `gh:owner/repo` with no `#number`.
   - owner or repo violating GitHub login/repo rules.
   - mixed-case schemes (only literal `gh#` and `gh:`).
3. Expose parsed refs on the `Erg` struct with a kind discriminator
   (`local | gh-same | gh-cross`). Downstream code must not
   re-parse the string.
4. Cycle check unchanged: cross-repo refs are terminal from this
   repo's view and cannot participate in local cycles.
5. No network calls. Cross-repo refs are accepted on syntax alone;
   referent existence is a runtime concern (0018).

## Tests

- Each form parses to the right kind.
- Malformed forms rejected, one test per failure mode.
- Existing `gh#N` fixtures still validate.
- Cycle detection still works with cross-repo refs in the mix.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `rules/tickets.md` documents the three-form grammar and the
      owner/repo rules.
- [ ] Deferred #1 (bare `gh#N` fork risk) decided in spec text.
- [ ] Validator parses all three forms, rejects malformed.
- [ ] `Erg` struct exposes `[]Ref{Kind, ...}` for blockers.
- [ ] Tests cover each form and each failure mode.
